    "front": "What is the significance of 'Aditya-L1'?",
    "back": "India's first solar mission, successfully placed in halo orbit around Lagrange Point 1 (L1)<br><br><div style='font-size:0.85em; text-align:left;'><ul style='margin-top:5px; padding-left:15px;'><li><b>Launch Vehicle:</b> PSLV-C57 (Launched Sept 2, 2023).</li><li><b>Location:</b> Halo orbit around L1 point (1.5 million km from Earth).</li><li><b>Payloads:</b> Carries 7 payloads (VELC, SUIT, etc.) to study photosphere, chromosphere, and corona.</li></ul></div><br><br><div style='font-size:0.85em; text-align:left;'><ul style='margin-top:5px; padding-left:15px;'><li><b>Launch Vehicle:</b> PSLV-C57 (Launched Sept 2, 2023).</li><li><b>Location:</b> Halo orbit around L1 point (1.5 million km from Earth).</li><li><b>Payloads:</b> Carries 7 payloads (VELC, SUIT, etc.) to study photosphere, chromosphere, and corona.</li></ul></div>"
